---
/**
 * Landing page — the front door. Lists the 5 lessons with
 * their through-lines and links to each.
 */
import LessonLayout from '../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const lessons = [
  { num: 1, slug: '01-syntax', title: 'Kotlin syntax — the foundations', tag: 'the one idea: less ceremony, more intent', desc: 'val/var, types, control flow as expressions, ranges, loops, default and named arguments. The pieces that show up in every program.' },
  { num: 2, slug: '02-classes-null-safety', title: 'Classes & null safety', tag: 'the one idea: make impossible states impossible', desc: 'Primary/secondary constructors, properties, visibility, and the null safety system: ?., ?:, smart casts, !!.' },
  { num: 3, slug: '03-data-modeling', title: 'Modeling data in Kotlin', tag: 'the one idea: constrain the set of legal values', desc: 'data class, sealed class, enum class, object, and companion object — one spectrum from "exactly one value" to "any of N data shapes."' },
  { num: 4, slug: '04-scope-functions', title: 'Extension & scope functions', tag: 'the one idea: temporarily change the context', desc: 'Extension functions as the engine, then let, apply, run, also, with on a 2×2: who is this and what does the block return.' },
  { num: 5, slug: '05-functional', title: 'Functional Kotlin', tag: 'the one idea: behavior as a value', desc: 'Lambdas, higher-order functions, and the collection ops (map, filter, reduce, groupBy) as pre-written HOFs.' },
];
---

<LessonLayout
  title="Kotlin, in five connected ideas"
  description="A series of five lessons on Kotlin — syntax, null safety, data modeling, scope functions, and functional style — each framed as one connected idea."
  number={0}
  primary="#2c5f5d"
  accent="#e8896b"
>
  <div class="eyebrow">Kotlin series · 5 lessons</div>
  <h1>Kotlin, in <em>five</em> connected ideas.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Each of these lessons is a tour of one part of the language — syntax, null
    safety, data modeling, scope functions, functional style. But they all
    share the same philosophy: <strong>remove ceremony, make the right thing
    easy, and let the type system do the work.</strong>
  </p>

  <div class="meta">
    <span>📚 5 lessons</span>
    <span>⏱ ~50 min total</span>
    <span>🎯 Beginner → intermediate</span>
  </div>

  <!-- Series arc -->
  <section class="arc" aria-label="Series overview">
    <div class="arc-title">The five lessons, in order</div>
    <div class="arc-track">
      <div class="arc-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="arc-nodes">
        {lessons.map((l) => (
          <a class="arc-node" href={`/${l.slug}/`}>
            <div class="arc-dot">{l.num}</div>
            <div class="arc-name">{l.title.split('—')[0].replace('& ', '').trim()}</div>
            <div class="arc-tag">{l.tag.replace('the one idea: ', '')}</div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2>Open a lesson</h2>
  <div class="lessons">
    {lessons.map((l) => (
      <a class="lesson" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}${l.slug}/`}>
        <div class="lesson-num">{String(l.num).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
        <div class="lesson-body">
          <h3 class="lesson-title">{l.title}</h3>
          <div class="lesson-tag">{l.tag}</div>
          <p class="lesson-desc">{l.desc}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lesson-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </div>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>

  <!-- One philosophy panel -->
  <section class="one-idea">
    <div class="tag">The through-line</div>
    <h2>One philosophy, five places it shows up.</h2>
    <p>
      Kotlin has a bias. It thinks the right thing should be the easy thing, and
      the wrong thing should be hard to write. The five lessons above are five
      different places that bias shows up.
    </p>
    <p>
      Syntax removes ceremony. Null safety makes bad states unrepresentable.
      Data modeling lets the type system know what's legal. Scope functions
      let you change context without changing identity. Functional style turns
      behavior into a value. Same goal, different surface.
    </p>
    <div class="one-idea-grid">
      <div class="one-idea-item"><div class="n">01</div><div class="t">Less ceremony, more intent.</div></div>
      <div class="one-idea-item"><div class="n">02</div><div class="t">Impossible states are impossible to write.</div></div>
      <div class="one-idea-item"><div class="n">03</div><div class="t">The type knows the set of legal values.</div></div>
      <div class="one-idea-item"><div class="n">04</div><div class="t">Context shifts are explicit and local.</div></div>
      <div class="one-idea-item"><div class="n">05</div><div class="t">Behavior is a value, like data.</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How to use -->
  <section class="howto">
    <h2>How to read this series</h2>
    <div class="howto-grid">
      <div class="howto-step">
        <div class="howto-num">1</div>
        <div class="howto-body">
          <h4>In order if you're new to Kotlin</h4>
          <p>Each lesson builds on the last. Syntax is the floor, functional is the ceiling. The order is the path.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="howto-step">
        <div class="howto-num">2</div>
        <div class="howto-body">
          <h4>Out of order if you're coming from another language</h4>
          <p>Already know Java or Swift? Start with whatever's most foreign. Null safety, sealed classes, and scope functions tend to be the new stuff.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="howto-step">
        <div class="howto-num">3</div>
        <div class="howto-body">
          <h4>As a reference later</h4>
          <p>Each lesson is self-contained. The recap at the end of each is meant to be skimmable on its own.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="howto-step">
        <div class="howto-num">4</div>
        <div class="howto-body">
          <h4>One at a time</h4>
          <p>Each is about 10–12 minutes of focused reading. Don't try to do all five in one sitting.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="end">
    Five lessons, one philosophy: <em>the right thing should be the easy thing.</em>
  </div>
</LessonLayout>

<style>
  .arc {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--r-2xl);
    padding: 40px 32px 32px;
    margin: 48px 0;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.03);
  }
  .arc-title {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .arc-track { position: relative; padding: 0 8px; }
  .arc-line {
    position: absolute;
    top: 24px; left: 24px; right: 24px;
    height: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent) 0%, var(--primary) 100%);
    z-index: 0;
  }
  .arc-nodes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    gap: 8px;
    position: relative; z-index: 1;
  }
  .arc-node {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    color: inherit;
    transition: transform 0.2s;
  }
  .arc-node:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .arc-dot {
    width: 50px; height: 50px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 3px solid var(--primary);
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--primary);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    transition: box-shadow 0.2s;
  }
  .arc-node:hover .arc-dot {
    box-shadow: 0 6px 16px -4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
  }
  .arc-name {
    font-family: "Outfit", sans-serif;
    font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .arc-tag {
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .arc-line { display: none; }
    .arc-nodes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; }
    .arc-node { flex-direction: row; gap: 16px; text-align: left; }
    .arc-dot { margin-bottom: 0; flex-shrink: 0; }
  }

  .lessons {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: 32px 0;
  }
  .lesson {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    padding: 24px 28px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr auto;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    align-items: center;
    color: inherit;
    transition: transform 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s, border-color 0.2s;
  }
  .lesson:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px -6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    border-color: var(--primary);
  }
  .lesson-num {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 36px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .lesson-body { min-width: 0; }
  .lesson-title {
    font-family: "DM Serif Display", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 24px;
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 4px;
  }
  .lesson-tag {
    font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-style: italic;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .lesson-desc {
    font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--ink-mid);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .lesson-arrow {
    width: 40px; height: 40px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--primary-soft);
    color: var(--primary);
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: background 0.2s, color 0.2s;
  }
  .lesson:hover .lesson-arrow { background: var(--primary); color: white; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .lesson { grid-template-columns: 50px 1fr; padding: 20px; }
    .lesson-arrow { display: none; }
    .lesson-num { font-size: 28px; }
    .lesson-title { font-size: 20px; }
  }

  .one-idea {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--primary) 0%, var(--primary-deep) 100%);
    color: white;
    border-radius: var(--r-xl);
    padding: 40px;
    margin: 48px 0;
  }
  .one-idea .tag {
    display: inline-block;
    color: #c3e88d;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 6px 14px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .one-idea h2 { color: white; margin: 0 0 16px; font-size: 32px; }
  .one-idea p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    font-size: 16px;
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .one-idea-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .one-idea-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .one-idea-item {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
    padding: var(--space-4);
  }
  .one-idea-item .n {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 11px; color: #c3e88d; margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .one-idea-item .t {
    font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);
  }

  .howto {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--r-xl);
    padding: var(--space-8);
    margin: 32px 0;
  }
  .howto h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .howto-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .howto-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .howto-step { display: flex; gap: 14px; }
  .howto-num {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 32px; height: 32px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--primary-soft);
    color: var(--primary);
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600;
  }
  .howto-body h4 {
    font-family: "Outfit", sans-serif;
    font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 4px; color: var(--ink);
  }
  .howto-body p {
    font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-mid);
    margin: 0; line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
